<h1>🟩 Fill Loops — English Worksheet</h1>
<p><strong>Topic:</strong> One corner, six rectangles · <strong>Course:</strong> 3D Coordinates · <strong>Level:</strong> Extension · <strong>Time:</strong> about 40 minutes</p>
<p><span class="timing">Type <code>del</code> before every <code>run</code>. Every time.</span></p>
<p>Every <code>???</code> is one short thing for you to work out. There are no answers on this sheet.</p>
<hr />
<h2>1 · Read the loop 🔍</h2>
<pre><code class="language-python">x_start = 1
z_start = 1
x_end = 1
z_end = 1
for i in range(1, 7):
    blocks.fill(EMERALD_BLOCK,
        pos(x_start, 0, z_start),
        pos(x_end, 0, z_end), REPLACE)
    x_end = x_end + 2
    z_end = z_end + 3
</code></pre>
<p><strong><code>range(1, 7)</code> gives you which numbers? Write them all.</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>Two lines inside the loop change a variable. Write them.</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>Four variables never change. Which?</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<div class="check"><span class="lab">Got it right if</span> your list of numbers stops at 6, not 7.</div>

<hr />
<h2>2 · Fill the table ✏️</h2>
<p>Do it in your head first. Run the code after.</p>
<table class="tr">
<tr><th>i</th><th>x_end</th><th>z_end</th><th>size</th><th>blocks</th></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1 x 1</td><td>1</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td>3</td><td>4</td><td>3 x 4</td><td>12</td></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr>
<tr><td>4</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr>
<tr><td>5</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr>
<tr><td>6</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr>
</table>

<p><strong>Add up the last column. How many blocks does the code write?</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>Now walk on your build and count it. How many blocks are really there?</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<div class="mini-q">The two numbers are different.</div>

<p><strong>Why?</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<hr />
<h2>3 · One fill instead of six 🎯</h2>
<p>Only the last rectangle is still visible.</p>
<div class="tpl">Template</div>

<pre><code class="language-python">blocks.fill(EMERALD_BLOCK,
    pos(1, 0, 1),
    pos(???, 0, ???), REPLACE)
</code></pre>
<div class="steps"><span class="lab">Steps</span>
<ol>
<li>Type <code>del</code>.</li>
<li>Run your one-line version.</li>
<li>Type <code>del</code>. Run the loop version.</li>
<li>Look at both. Same shape?</li>
</ol>
</div>

<div class="check"><span class="lab">Works when</span> both builds look exactly the same.</div>

<hr />
<h2>4 · Make it stand up 🧱</h2>
<p>Right now <code>y_start</code> and <code>y_end</code> are both <code>0</code>, so your build is one block tall.</p>
<div class="tpl">Template · inside the loop</div>

<pre><code class="language-python">    x_end = x_end + 2
    z_end = z_end + 3
    ??? = ??? + ???
</code></pre>
<div class="warn"><span class="lab">Start small</span>
Use <b>1</b> first. Adding 3 six times makes it 15 tall and your <code>del</code> cannot reach the top.</div>

<p><strong>Before you run it: how tall will it be after 6 turns if you add 1 each time?</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<div class="check"><span class="lab">Works when</span> it is a solid block you can stand next to, not a floor.</div>

<hr />
<h2>5 · Pull them apart ✂️</h2>
<p>The near corner never moves, so the shapes sit on top of each other. Move it and they separate.</p>
<div class="tpl">Template · inside the loop</div>

<pre><code class="language-python">    ??? = ??? + ???
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Tree of thought: tree 3 is 5 wide. How far must the corner move so shapes do not touch?</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<div class="check"><span class="lab">Works when</span> you can walk between the shapes.</div>

<div class="stuck"><span class="lab">Still one lump?</span>
You changed <code>x_end</code> again instead of <code>x_start</code>. Read the variable name carefully.</div>

<hr />
<h2>6 · Show Your Work 📸🎥</h2>
<p>Record <strong>one video</strong>, one take, no stopping. A phone is fine. Show these in order:</p>
<blockquote>
<ol>
<li>Type <code>del</code>, then <code>run</code>. Walk around your build.</li>
<li>Show the two lines inside the loop and say what each one does.</li>
<li>Show your filled table and say why the two totals are different.</li>
<li>Show your one-line version next to the loop version.</li>
<li>Show your standing-up build and say which variable you changed.</li>
</ol>
</blockquote>
<p>Try to use these words: <strong>loop</strong>, <strong>variable</strong>, <strong>corner</strong>, <strong>fill</strong>, <strong>cover</strong>.</p>
<p><strong>Plan what you will say before you record.</strong></p>
